.TITLE "head"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the beginning of a file or piped data. By default, it shows the __first 10 lines__, making it useful for quickly inspecting the structure or headers of a file.

.DIV "TLDR"
**head file**
Displays the first 10 lines of the specified file.
> __file__ the target file

**head -n number file**
Displays a custom number of lines from the start of the file.
> __-n__ line count flag | __number__ how many lines to show | __file__ target file

**head -c bytes file**
Displays the first specific number of bytes from the file.
> __-c__ byte count flag | __bytes__ how many bytes to show | __file__ target file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __head__ is a fast way to verify you are working with the correct file without loading its entire content. Combining it with __grep__ or __sort__ can help you isolate the most relevant data at the top of a list.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:tail** **linux:cat** **linux:sed**

